": -0.5, "poll_sd": 10.5, "poll_weight": 0.19, "fundamentals": {"margin": -1.0, "lean": -6.0, "environment": 7.9, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": -0.9}, "rating_margin": -12.11, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.66, "baseline_margin": -6.29, "analyst_adjustment": -2.71, "key_factors": ["R+6 district with incumbent Mike Flood running and a large fundraising edge ($2.4M vs $0.6M)", "Expert ratings cluster Likely/Solid R, implying roughly a 12-point Republican margin", "A single September Democratic-sponsored poll shows a one-point race, but it is an outlier against the fundamentals", "Polymarket prices Flood around an 82% win probability"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a mid-single-digit Republican margin in an R+6 seat with a well-funded incumbent, while the rating consensus and prediction markets suggest a wider lead; the lone recent Democratic-sponsored poll showing a tied race is thin evidence to lean on. A blend lands around a nine-point Flood edge, keeping the race Likely R rather than Safe R.", "watch": "The late-September debate and any follow-up polling confirming or refuting the tied September survey could shift the race toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Flood (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Nebraska's 1st District leans Republican by about six points, and first-term incumbent Mike Flood is seeking re-election with a decisive financial advantage, having raised roughly four times as much as Democrat Chris Backemeyer. Most professional raters place the seat in the Likely or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Flood about an 82% chance of winning.\n\nThe race's main wrinkle is a September poll from a Democratic-sponsored firm showing the contest essentially tied, far more competitive than the fundamentals imply. Backemeyer has modest outside support and the two candidates are scheduled to debate, but with little independent polling and a strong incumbent, Flood remains the clear favorite, with some room for the race to tighten.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1466, "margin": -6.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0854, "margin": -9.0}]}